{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: identify y'' + y = 0\nidentify y'' + y = 0:\n  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)\n  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]\n  homogeneous\n  constant coefficients (and autonomous)\n  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i\n  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)\n  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly\n  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what kind of equation is y'' + y = 0?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["identify y'' + y = 0"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "identify", "input": "y'' + y = 0", "properties": {"linear": {"text": "every y-term appears to the first power", "tag": "proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y", "proof": "symbolic"}, "characteristic_equation": "r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i", "homogeneous_solutions": "y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)", "autonomous": "the independent variable does not appear explicitly", "solved_for_the_highest_derivative": "y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)", "details": ["an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)", "homogeneous", "constant coefficients (and autonomous)"]}}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: identify y'' + y = 0\nidentify y'' + y = 0:\n  an ordinary differential equation of order 2 in y(t)\n  linear: every y-term appears to the first power [proved: the partial derivatives in y, y', ... do not involve y]\n  homogeneous\n  constant coefficients (and autonomous)\n  characteristic equation: r^2 + 1 = 0, roots ±i\n  homogeneous solutions: y(t) = a combination of cos(t), sin(t)\n  autonomous: the independent variable does not appear explicitly\n  solved for the highest derivative: y'' = -y  (then initial values and: dsolve y)\n"}, "isError": false}}
